  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-codec-haproxy 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-codec-haproxy 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-44893, CVE-2026-48059, CVE-2026-55851, and CVE-2026-59919.\n\nCVE-2026-44893: Netty: HAProxy SSL TLV parsing leaks retained slice on invalid TLV length\n\nCVE-2026-48059: Netty HAProxy: Unbalanced Reference Count in Nested PP2_TYPE_SSL TLV Parsing Leads to Memory Exhaustion\n\nCVE-2026-55851: Netty codec-haproxy: Signed-Byte Sentinel Collision in HAProxyMessageDecoder Leads to Unbounded Memory Exhaustion\n\nCVE-2026-59919: Netty: HAProxy V1 Protocol CRLF Injection via AF_UNIX Address\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-codec-haproxy 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
